{"type":"text","timestamp":1794861604835,"sessionID":"ses_e19eaf816ffeLK63YQCC74Krze","part":{"id":"prt_1e6169b1e001m4CDHBlWkbFEls","messageID":"msg_1e61696ef001VijpJ50rizXyCb","sessionID":"ses_e19eaf816ffeLK63YQCC74Krze","type":"text","text":"Upgrade complete.\n\n**Changes**\n- `vendor/moneyfmt/__init__.py` — replaced with the 2.0.0 release, byte-identical to `vendor-updates/moneyfmt-2.0.0/moneyfmt/__init__.py` (verified with `diff -r`).\n- `requirements.txt` — pin now `moneyfmt==2.0.0`.\n- `invoicer/totals.py:7` — `MoneyError` → `MoneyFormatError`; `Line.amount` is now `Decimal` (`invoicer/totals.py:20`); `total()` returns `Decimal` seeded with `Decimal(\"0\")` so an empty invoice still formats (`invoicer/totals.py:36`); `format_money(..., currency=CURRENCY)` is now keyword-only (`invoicer/totals.py:40`).\n- `tests/test_totals.py` — added `Moneyfmt2ApiTest` (pins/vendor version check, `parse_money` returns `Decimal`, old `MoneyError` name gone, `format_money` rejects float/positional currency, invoicer calls it with `Decimal` + keyword currency, exact decimal total) and `CliTest` (CLI stdout/stderr/exit-status parity).\n\n**Behavior**\n- All 11 tests pass; CLI output, error messages and exit codes match the pre-upgrade baseline byte-for-byte, except the stated allowed difference: three `1.005` lines now total `€3.02` instead of `€3.01`.\n- One unavoidable library-driven change: `NaN`/`Infinity` amounts are now rejected by `parse_money`, so they produce `error: cannot read amount 'NaN'` with exit 2 instead of the previous unhandled `decimal.InvalidOperation` traceback (exit 1).","time":{"start":1794861603614,"end":1794861604833}}}
